    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> be two real numbers such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mi>&#945;</mi></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mi>&#946;</mi></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>29</mn></math> for some integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#10878;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Then, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math> is______."
  },
